What is abstraction?
Abstraction means hiding complicated details and showing only what the user needs to use.

class Car:
    def start(self):
        self._check_engine()
        self._inject_fuel()
        self._start_engine()

    def _check_engine(self):
        print("Checking engine...")

    def _inject_fuel(self):
        print("Injecting fuel...")

    def _start_engine(self):
        print("Engine started!")
As the user, you just do:

car = Car()
car.start()

Python example
from abc import ABC,abstractmethod
class animal(ABC):
    @abstractmethod
    def sound(self):
        pass
class Dog(animal):
    def sound(self):
        print("woof")
class Cat(animal):
    def sound(self):
        print("meow")
cat=Cat()
dog=Dog()
print(cat.sound())
print(dog.sound())

